WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
Jewish tradition counts 613
commandments in the Torah,

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.150
given at Mount Sinai.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.520
In 1967, Emil Fackenheim, a
rabbi once held in a Nazi camp,

4
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.570
proposed one more: number 614.

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.230
He said it came from Auschwitz,
as a commanding voice.

6
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.980
But what could a commandment that comes
from Auschwitz possibly command a Jew

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.450
to do?

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.590
In this mission, you'll set his answer beside
other Jewish responses to the Holocaust.

9
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.730
Then you'll ask whether any theology
can speak about the Holocaust at all,

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.060
or whether silence is better.

11
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: find out what this
new commandment demands, and why.
